    "display_name": "Astronomy",
    "long_instructions": "For a science class, you’ve been asked to find out how long it takes for planets to orbit the Sun based on how far away they are. You have a file with each planet's average distance from the sun (in millions of kilometers) and the length of its year in days. \r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Import the `csv` module.\r\n2. Call the `open` function to open the `planets.csv` file.\r\n3. Read the file with `csv.DictReader`.\r\n4. Loop through the data. The `distance` value is already printed for you. Add a line to print the `days` value too. Compare your printed output to the CSV file. Do the numbers match?\r\n5. Close the file.\r\n",
